<main>
<h1>2021miyagi-okiL / kiban · Seismicity and repeaters</h1>
<div class="controls">
<label>Latitude band <select id="band"><option value="all">All: 38–38.75°N</option><option value="0">38–38.25°N</option><option value="1">38.25–38.5°N</option><option value="2">38.5–38.75°N</option></select></label>
<label>Time-plot symbol size <input id="size" type="range" min="0.3" max="3" step="0.1" value="1"><output id="sizeValue">1.0×</output></label>
<label>Color <select id="colorMode"><option value="depth" selected>Depth</option><option value="latitude">Latitude</option><option value="type">Event type</option></select></label>
<label>Minimum M ≥ <input id="mmin" type="range" min="1.5" max="6" step="0.1" value="1.5"><output id="mValue">1.5</output></label>
<label><input id="background" type="checkbox" checked>Background events</label>
<button id="reset">Reset view</button>
</div>
<p class="hint">Scroll to zoom around the cursor · Drag to pan · Double-click to reset<br>Map and lower panel share longitude; map and right panel share latitude; the two time panels share time. Map circles show fault radii at 32 MPa and scale with zoom. Magnitude differences are emphasized in both time plots, using M=3 as the reference. The slider changes symbols in both time plots. Click an event to pin its details.</p>
<div id="typeLegend" class="legend"><span><i class="dot" style="background:#999"></i>Background events</span><span><i class="dot" style="background:#168a96"></i>Repeater</span><span style="color:#ce6138">M_JMA ≥ 6 (stars)</span><span>Dashed line: 2011-03-11</span></div>
<div id="latitudeLegend" style="margin:12px 0">Latitude (°N): 38 <span style="display:inline-block;width:200px;height:12px;background:linear-gradient(to right,#440154,#3b528b,#21918c,#5ec962,#fde725);vertical-align:middle;margin:0 8px"></span> 38.75<br><small>Repeaters: stronger outlines; background events: lighter outlines. M_JMA ≥ 6: stars in all panels; orange stars mark map epicenters. Time-panel dashed line: 2011-03-11. Map rectangle: analysis bounds.</small></div>
<div id="depthLegend" style="margin:12px 0">Depth (km): <span id="depthMin"></span> <span style="display:inline-block;width:200px;height:12px;background:linear-gradient(to right,#440154,#3b528b,#21918c,#5ec962,#fde725);vertical-align:middle;margin:0 8px"></span> <span id="depthMax"></span><br><small>Shallow → deep. Repeaters have stronger outlines. Stars: M_JMA ≥ 6. Dashed time line: 2011-03-11.</small></div>
<div class="map-row"><div class="plot"><canvas id="map" aria-label="Earthquake locations in longitude and latitude"></canvas></div><div class="plot"><canvas id="latTime" aria-label="Earthquake year versus latitude"></canvas></div></div>
<div class="controls"><label>Time-plot symbol size <input id="sizeBetween" type="range" min="0.3" max="3" step="0.1" value="1"><output id="sizeBetweenValue">1.0×</output></label></div>
<div class="map-row"><div class="plot"><canvas id="time" aria-label="Earthquake longitude versus year"></canvas></div><div aria-hidden="true"></div></div>
<div id="selected">Click an event to show its details here.</div>
<p id="counts"></p>
<small>Catalogue bounds: 141.4–142.05°E, 38–38.75°N, depth 0–100 km, M ≥ 1.5. Only events within ±10 km vertically of the plate boundary are included. All identified repeater sequences are included.<br>Map: circular-crack radius at 32 MPa; M₀ = 10^(1.5 M + 9.1) N m, using catalogue M as an Mw proxy, as in mag2size3. Map circles show equivalent physical fault size, not mapped rupture outlines. Time plot: visual magnitude scaling. Data are embedded for offline use. Map lines: coastline (solid), prefecture boundaries (thin dashed), and analysis bounds (bold dashed rectangle). The map preserves local east–west and north–south distance proportions.</small>
